  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"schemabench_0209\" consists of 10 tables. The primary purpose of this database is to manage and track various aspects of a student's education, including student information, course details, enrollments, classes, attendance, grades, teacher information, teaching assignments, department details, and student department assignments.\nThe \"students\" table holds information about each student, including their first and last names, middle name, date of birth, email, phone number, address, and a description. The \"courses\" table contains details about each course, including the course name, course code, creation date, credit hours, and a description.\nThe \"enrollments\" table is used to track student enrollments in different courses. It references the \"students\" and \"courses\" tables, allowing us to know which student is enrolled in which course.\nThe \"classes\" table contains information about the classes, including the course they belong to, class name, class schedule, class room, and a description. This table also references the \"courses\" table, establishing a link between classes and courses.\nThe \"attendance\" table records attendance information for each class, including the class, student, attendance date, status, and a description. It references the \"classes\" and \"students\" tables to link the attendance records to the respective class and student.\nThe \"grades\" table is used to store grades for each enrollment, including the marks obtained, total marks, grade, and a description. It references the \"enrollments\" table to link grades to the respective enrollment.\nThe \"teachers\" table contains information about the teachers, including their first and last names, middle name, email, phone number, address, and a description. The \"teaching_assignments\" table is used to track which teacher is assigned to which class. It references both the \"teachers\" and \"classes\" tables.\nThe \"departments\" table holds information about the departments, including the department name and a description. The \"student_department\" table is used to track which student belongs to which department. It references both the \"students\" and \"departments\" tables.\nThis schema ensures data integrity by enforcing primary and foreign key constraints, which prevent inconsistencies and ensure referential integrity. It also allows for easy updates and deletions, as cascade and restrict actions are defined on foreign key constraints.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project is focused on developing a comprehensive database system for managing student records and associated academic activities. This database, known as `StudentManagement`, is designed to handle various aspects of student data, including courses, grades, attendance, and departmental affiliations.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe primary objective is to implement a robust database framework that facilitates efficient management of student information, course enrollments, grading systems, and attendance tracking. The system should provide functionalities for student registration, record maintenance, and academic performance evaluation.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Students: Access their personal and academic information.\n- Teachers: Manage class schedules, assignments, and record student performance.\n- Administrators: Oversee the database, manage student enrollments, and ensure data integrity.\n- Departments: Monitor departmental data and student affiliations.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Student Registration: \n   - Functions to add, update, and manage student personal and contact information.\n   - Linking students to their respective departments.\n\n2. Course Management:\n   - Creation and management of courses, including course schedules and room assignments.\n\n3. Enrollment Management:\n   - Enroll students in courses and maintain enrollment records.\n\n4. Grade Tracking:\n   - Record student grades and calculate their academic performance based on obtained marks.\n\n5. Attendance Tracking:\n   - Maintain attendance records for students in each class.\n\n6. Teaching Assignments:\n   - Manage teacher assignments to classes and provide relevant class information.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Support a growing number of student records and courses without degradation in performance.\n- Data Integrity: Ensure consistency and accuracy of student and academic records.\n- Security: Protect sensitive student data from unauthorized access.\n- Availability: The system should be available for access by students, teachers, and administrators at all required times.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0209.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0209\nCREATE TABLE `students` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `middle_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `courses` (\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `course_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `course_code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `credit_hours` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`course_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `enrollments` (\n  `enrollment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`enrollment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `enrollments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `students` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `enrollments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `courses` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `classes` (\n  `class_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `class_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `class_schedule` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `class_room` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`class_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `classes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `courses` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `attendance` (\n  `attendance_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `class_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `attendance_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`attendance_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `attendance_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`class_id`) REFERENCES `classes` (`class_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `attendance_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `students` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `grades` (\n  `grade_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `enrollment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `marks_obtained` float NOT NULL,\n  `total_marks` float NOT NULL,\n  `grade` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`grade_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `grades_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`enrollment_id`) REFERENCES `enrollments` (`enrollment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `teachers` (\n  `teacher_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `middle_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`teacher_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `teaching_assignments` (\n  `assignment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `teacher_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `class_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`assignment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `teaching_assignments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`teacher_id`) REFERENCES `teachers` (`teacher_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `teaching_assignments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`class_id`) REFERENCES `classes` (`class_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `departments` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `department_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `student_department` (\n  `student_department_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_department_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `student_department_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `students` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `student_department_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `departments` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
